1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Money complaints reach support by call, ticket and email, in many languages.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
A shop owner says, in Hindi, that rent is still cut after the Soundbox went back.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Munim follows the money: ledger, mandate, device, pickup.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The AI asked for ₹1,497. The rules recomputed ₹998 from the ledger and refunded that.

5
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The reply is in Hindi and waits as a draft. Nothing reaches the merchant until a person presses Send.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Same bug found in 36 more merchants (₹32,029) before they complain. A person reviews each one.

7
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Charged twice for one device: ₹2,495. That's over the ₹2,000 auto-limit, so a person approves.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Fake admin demands ₹50,000. No evidence, so it is blocked.

9
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:00,000
No known cause fits. The AI writes read-only SQL, finds a chargeback and hands it to the payments team.

10
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:12,000
A bus turned back at km 38, but the operator never marked it cancelled.

11
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:25,000
GPS and the driver's report prove it. The ₹1,640 fare is refunded, and 18 more passengers are found.

12
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:45,000
The airline paid the ₹21,860 refund on 3 Oct, but it was never matched to the booking. A person approves it. 8 more passengers are found.

13
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Shop owners can ask Munim directly. It can book a pickup, but it never moves money from the app.

14
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:12,000
AI proposes. Code decides. A person signs off on big money.
